arm: cast to char* when clearing the icache

clang rejects passing `address` (unsigned char*) to __builtin___clear_cache,
which takes char*:

  icache_arm.cpp:33:27: error: cannot initialize a parameter of type 'char *'
  with an lvalue of type 'address' (aka 'unsigned char *')

gcc is lenient here, so this only shows up on the clang-built arm targets --
which is all of ours, since the NDK is clang.

From termux-packages openjdk-25 patch 0012 (Henrik Grimler).

diff --git a/src/hotspot/cpu/arm/icache_arm.cpp b/src/hotspot/cpu/arm/icache_arm.cpp
index 61fcb8a..93d2ad4 100644
--- a/src/hotspot/cpu/arm/icache_arm.cpp
+++ b/src/hotspot/cpu/arm/icache_arm.cpp
@@ -31,7 +31,7 @@
 
 
 static int icache_flush(address addr, int lines, int magic) {
-  __builtin___clear_cache(addr, addr + (lines << ICache::log2_line_size));
+  __builtin___clear_cache((char*) addr, (char*) (addr + (lines << ICache::log2_line_size)));
   return magic;
 }
 
